I'm still not convinced that using numbers for this sort of thing is a good
idea. The scale is of course totally arbitrary, so the apparent exactness
of "7 out of 10" is illusory, since most people would disagree how good
that is. On the other hand, words like "mildly", "moderately", etc. are
equally as vague, but they don't have the false facade of exact numbers.


